  //  Exponentiation
  The cartesian form takes integer exponents without difficulty.
  Yet it soon becomes tedious:

    z  =  a + jb

    =>    z³  =  (a + jb) (a + jb) (a + jb)

              =  (a² + jab + jab — b²) (a + jb)

              =  (a² + 2jab — b²) (a + jb)

              =  a³ + ja²b + 2ja²b — 2ab² — ab² — jb³

              =  a³  —  3ab²  +  j (3a²b — jb³)

  Ok. But what about z¹⁷⁷⁰ or z¹‧⁶¹⁸⁰³³⁹⁸⁹ ?
  We're dealing with exponentiation —— and we have access to an exponential form.
  Let's use it.
                ________
       |z|  =  √ a² + b²
    arg(z)  =  atan2(b, a)

    z  =  |z| exp( j arg(z) )

